; bfsodium MULMOD136 : (a times b) modulo p = 2^130 minus 5
;
; HAND WRITTEN; double and add  lowest bit of b first; acc starts at nought and
; t starts at a  and on each of the 136 turns: if b's low bit is set then acc
; gains t  t doubles  and b shifts down one; After 136 turns every bit of b has
; had its say  and one reduction at the end brings the answer below p;
;
; INTERFACE entry=34 exit=0 footprint=0:286
; IO  in:  a{17} LE  followed by  b{17} LE     (34 bytes)
;     out: (a times b mod p){17} LE            (17 bytes)
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x060  the work frame; every pasted routine runs HERE  at this file's
;                 own zero  and the operands are carried to it and back; the
;                 frame is 0:96 because reducep136 is the largest of them
;   @0x0c8:0x0d8  acc{17}   the answer being accumulated
;   @0x0dc:0x0ec  t{17}     a doubled once per turn  reduced each time
;   @0x0f0:0x100  bv{17}    b  shifted down one per turn until it is gone
;   @0x104:0x114  tmp{17}   hands t back after it has been copied
;   @0x118        h         HALVE frame: a copy of bv's low byte
;   @0x119        q         HALVE frame: that byte shifted right one  discarded
;   @0x11a        bit       HALVE frame: that byte low bit  which is b's bit
;   @0x11b        f         HALVE frame scratch  restored to nought
;   @0x11e        n         136 turns
;
; NOTHING here is reduced by the adder twice over: t doubles with dbl136  which
; costs about half a million instructions  where add136 on two full values costs
; about twelve million because its cost is the PRODUCT of the byte values it is
; adding; Doubling is a shift and should cost what a shift costs;
;
; Every value stays under 2^130 plus fifteen between turns  because fold136 is
; applied after each add and after each double; So acc plus t stays under 2^131
; and the doubling never loses the bit it drops;
;
; a is folded ONCE before the loop; it arrives as any seventeen byte value  and
; doubling one of those would lose its top bit;

; read a{0:16} then b{0:16}  leaving the pointer past both
  ,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>
